(7582716, 1218521, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> I relly like this, but feel that if a lower angle would help it. you have the smoothness of the waters, but then the sharpness of the sky and buildings maybe if shot t half the angle you are at now, it would all be cohesive. But then again, I am no expert. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment. Funny, but I had one from a lower angle that I liked better but I got overruled by my team. This is a better "scape" shot for sure, while I think the other is the better photograph. If I dropped down 4 feet from here the trees get in the way so you have to move left and then you lose the street.</td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN: I relly like this, but feel that if a lower angle would help it. you have the smoothness of the waters, but then the sharpness of the sky and buildings maybe if shot t half the angle you are at now, it would all be cohesive. But then again, I am no expert.   Thanks for the comment. Funny, but I had one from a lower angle that I liked better but I got overruled by my team. This is a better "scape" shot for sure, while I think the other is the better photograph. If I dropped down 4 feet from here the trees get in the way so you have to move left and then you lose the street.', '2018-07-16 06:15:47.000000', NULL, 0),
